{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2096","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2096","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2096\",\"parent_revision\":\"6acff82a9c143481b3f7ce7e7c3e1b04b72799d5\",\"root_revision\":\"ea09a72d4b5e0a70a6b01fcfdac28a060e38874e8b77b9fc96c45fb2eb58471d\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nVerified against primary sources on 2026-05-04:\\\\n\\\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` lines 58-67: PostToolUse handler confirmed, matcher is `Write|Edit|Bash`, runs `task_status_hook.py` with 10-second timeout. VERIFIED.\\\\n- `task_status_hook.py` line 853: `handle_activity_update` is the sole PostToolUse handler. Lines 895-902: only action is writing `last-activity` timestamp via `sam_update_plan_fields`. Grep for `classify`, `observation`, `confidence` returns no matches outside LastActivity context. VERIFIED.\\\\n- `task_status_hook.py` lines 929-933: `main()` dispatches PostToolUse only to `handle_activity_update` for `{Write, Edit, Bash}`. VERIFIED.\\\\n- `research/context-management/claude-brain.md` lines 72-87: 10 observation types (`discovery`, `decision`, `problem`, `solution`, `pattern`, `warning`, `success`, `refactor`, `bugfix`, `feature`). SOURCE: src/types.ts lines 18-29. VERIFIED.\\\\n- `research/context-management/claude-brain.md` lines 206-208: `minConfidence: 0.6` default. SOURCE: src/types.ts lines 78-84. VERIFIED.\\\\n- `research/context-management/claude-brain.md` lines 178-185: PostToolUse hook captures, compresses, and deduplicates with 1-minute window. VERIFIED.\\\\n- `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/observations/` directory: does NOT currently exist \u2014 it must be created by the implementation. VERIFIED (directory not present).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Resources\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|---|---|\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json (lines 58-67 \u2014 PostToolUse registration pattern) |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py (lines 853-933 \u2014 PostToolUse handler to extend or register alongside) |\\n| Research | research/context-management/claude-brain.md (10-type classification schema, dedup window, minConfidence pattern) |\\n| Skill | /dh:implementation-manager (context file mechanism, dh_paths slug resolution) |\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Blocks: #1677 (PreCompact context preservation) and #1678 (periodic auto-save) cannot deliver intent-searchable context without typed observation records\\n- Bottleneck: Every PostToolUse event is reduced to a timestamp; no downstream consumer can query \\\"what bugs were fixed in this session\\\" or \\\"what discoveries were made\\\"\\n- Repeated tool calls in tight loops generate N timestamp writes instead of one deduplicated record\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Depends on: None (self-contained hook extension)\\n- Blocks: #1677 (PreCompact context preservation \u2014 needs observation records to be queryable by type), #1678 (periodic auto-save \u2014 same reason)\\n- Related: #1944 (stalled-task detection uses LastActivity \u2014 the existing LastActivity write path must not be disrupted by this change)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 This is the missing capture layer for the observation pipeline. Items #1677 and #1678 (both P1, groomed) will produce raw snapshots, but without per-tool-call typed observations those snapshots are unsearchable by intent. The classification gap means session knowledge is lost at the boundary between \\\"something happened\\\" and \\\"what happened\\\".\\n</div>\\n\\n## Benefits\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Enables intent-searchable session history (query by `discovery`, `bugfix`, `solution` etc.)\\n- Completes the observation pipeline that #1677 and #1678 depend on for queryability\\n- Eliminates redundant timestamp writes from identical successive tool calls (dedup window)\\n- Aligns the development harness with the claude-brain observation capture pattern, enabling future integration\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. After running a Claude Code session that performs at least one `Grep` and one `Edit`, `ls ~/.dh/projects/-home-user-claude_skills/observations/` lists a `<session-id>.jsonl` file\\n2. `cat <session-id>.jsonl | jq -r '.type' | sort -u` includes at least one of: `discovery`, `solution`, `bugfix`\\n3. Every record in the JSONL contains a `confidence` field with a float value\\n4. Running the same `Bash` command twice within 60 seconds produces one JSONL record with `count: 2`, not two records\\n5. Running the same `Bash` command twice with a gap > 60 seconds produces two JSONL records\\n6. No record with `confidence < 0.6` appears in the output file\\n7. The observation record type is defined as a Pydantic model or TypedDict \u2014 grep of the implementation for `cast(` or `: Any` returns zero matches on the record construction path\\n8. The `type` field is typed as a `Literal` union of the 10 allowed values \u2014 not bare `str`\\n9. `uv run prek run --files <implementation-file>` exits 0\\n10. If implemented as a sibling hook, `hooks.json` registers it alongside the existing PostToolUse handler without removing the existing LastActivity handler\\n</div>\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAfter each `Write`, `Edit`, or `Bash` PostToolUse event, the hook classifies the tool output into one of 10 typed observation categories using rule-based heuristics. Observations with confidence >= 0.6 are persisted as JSONL records in `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/observations/<session-id>.jsonl`. Identical tool calls within a 60-second window produce one record with a `count` field incremented, not N separate records. Records that fall below the confidence threshold are silently dropped.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nMedium \u2014 the classification heuristics are the primary complexity (rule-based pattern matching on tool output text). The JSONL write path, dedup window (in-memory dict keyed by `(tool_name, hash(input))`), and hook registration are each straightforward. The type safety constraint (Pydantic model, Literal union) adds bounded design work. Estimated 1\u20132 focused sessions.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **posttooluse observation classification and capture beyond lastactivity timestamp** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/context-management/claude-brain.md \u2014 pattern: Automatic observation capture with 10-type classification + dedup window\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-02\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Desired Structure\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA JSONL file at `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/observations/<session-id>.jsonl` exists after any session that performed at least one `Write`, `Edit`, or `Bash` tool call. Each line is a valid JSON object with fields: `id`, `timestamp`, `tool`, `type` (one of the 10 literals), `summary`, `confidence` (float 0.0-1.0), `metadata.session_id`. A second invocation with the same tool and input within 60 seconds produces a single record with `count: 2` rather than two records.\\n\\nThe observation record shape must be defined as a Pydantic model or TypedDict with `total=True` \u2014 not `dict[str, Any]`. The `type` field must use a `Literal` union of the 10 allowed values, not bare `str`. The `confidence` field must be typed `float` with a range constraint (0.0\u20131.0). Using `cast` or `Any` to construct or serialize the record is prohibited.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-04)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING**\\\\n\\\\nAll required inputs are present from primary sources. No human input needed.\\\\n\\\\n| Input | Status | Source |\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Item description \u2014 extend hook to classify and persist observations |\\\\n| Scope boundaries | AVAILABLE | 10 type values, 1-min dedup window, 0.6 min_confidence, JSONL output path |\\\\n| External interfaces | AVAILABLE | hooks.json lines 58-67, task_status_hook.py lines 853-933 |\\\\n| Constraints | AVAILABLE | 10-second hook timeout \u2192 rule-based only; PEP 723 Python 3.11+; uv run --script |\\\\n| Existing system context | AVAILABLE | context file mechanism confirmed; dh_paths slug resolution in use |\\\\n| Verification expectations | AVAILABLE | Measurable Signal section specifies exact commands and expected output |\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 This is the missing capture layer for the observation pipeline. Items #1677 and #1678 (both P1, groomed) will produce raw snapshots, but without per-tool-call typed observations those snapshots are unsearchable by intent. The classification gap means session knowledge is lost at the boundary between \\\"something happened\\\" and \\\"what happened\\\".\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: #1677 (PreCompact context preservation) and #1678 (periodic auto-save) cannot deliver intent-searchable context without typed observation records\\\\n- Bottleneck: Every PostToolUse event is reduced to a timestamp; no downstream consumer can query \\\"what bugs were fixed in this session\\\" or \\\"what discoveries were made\\\"\\\\n- Repeated tool calls in tight loops generate N timestamp writes instead of one deduplicated record\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Enables intent-searchable session history (query by `discovery`, `bugfix`, `solution` etc.)\\\\n- Completes the observation pipeline that #1677 and #1678 depend on for queryability\\\\n- Eliminates redundant timestamp writes from identical successive tool calls (dedup window)\\\\n- Aligns the development harness with the claude-brain observation capture pattern, enabling future integration\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nAfter each `Write`, `Edit`, or `Bash` PostToolUse event, the hook classifies the tool output into one of 10 typed observation categories using rule-based heuristics. Observations with confidence >= 0.6 are persisted as JSONL records in `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/observations/<session-id>.jsonl`. Identical tool calls within a 60-second window produce one record with a `count` field incremented, not N separate records. Records that fall below the confidence threshold are silently dropped.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nA JSONL file at `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/observations/<session-id>.jsonl` exists after any session that performed at least one `Write`, `Edit`, or `Bash` tool call. Each line is a valid JSON object with fields: `id`, `timestamp`, `tool`, `type` (one of the 10 literals), `summary`, `confidence` (float 0.0-1.0), `metadata.session_id`. A second invocation with the same tool and input within 60 seconds produces a single record with `count: 2` rather than two records.\\\\n\\\\nThe observation record shape must be defined as a Pydantic model or TypedDict with `total=True` \u2014 not `dict[str, Any]`. The `type` field must use a `Literal` union of the 10 allowed values, not bare `str`. The `confidence` field must be typed `float` with a range constraint (0.0\u20131.0). Using `cast` or `Any` to construct or serialize the record is prohibited.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. After running a Claude Code session that performs at least one `Grep` and one `Edit`, `ls ~/.dh/projects/-home-user-claude_skills/observations/` lists a `<session-id>.jsonl` file\\\\n2. `cat <session-id>.jsonl | jq -r '.type' | sort -u` includes at least one of: `discovery`, `solution`, `bugfix`\\\\n3. Every record in the JSONL contains a `confidence` field with a float value\\\\n4. Running the same `Bash` command twice within 60 seconds produces one JSONL record with `count: 2`, not two records\\\\n5. Running the same `Bash` command twice with a gap > 60 seconds produces two JSONL records\\\\n6. No record with `confidence < 0.6` appears in the output file\\\\n7. The observation record type is defined as a Pydantic model or TypedDict \u2014 grep of the implementation for `cast(` or `: Any` returns zero matches on the record construction path\\\\n8. The `type` field is typed as a `Literal` union of the 10 allowed values \u2014 not bare `str`\\\\n9. `uv run prek run --files <implementation-file>` exits 0\\\\n10. If implemented as a sibling hook, `hooks.json` registers it alongside the existing PostToolUse handler without removing the existing LastActivity handler\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\\\n|---|---|\\\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json (lines 58-67 \u2014 PostToolUse registration pattern) |\\\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py (lines 853-933 \u2014 PostToolUse handler to extend or register alongside) |\\\\n| Research | research/context-management/claude-brain.md (10-type classification schema, dedup window, minConfidence pattern) |\\\\n| Skill | /dh:implementation-manager (context file mechanism, dh_paths slug resolution) |\\\\n| Agent | @dh:fact-checker (verified claims in this item) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None (self-contained hook extension)\\\\n- Blocks: #1677 (PreCompact context preservation \u2014 needs observation records to be queryable by type), #1678 (periodic auto-save \u2014 same reason)\\\\n- Related: #1944 (stalled-task detection uses LastActivity \u2014 the existing LastActivity write path must not be disrupted by this change)\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\nNone \u2014 all inputs are present. The implementation can proceed directly to planning.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 the classification heuristics are the primary complexity (rule-based pattern matching on tool output text). The JSONL write path, dedup window (in-memory dict keyed by `(tool_name, hash(input))`), and hook registration are each straightforward. The type safety constraint (Pydantic model, Literal union) adds bounded design work. Estimated 1\u20132 focused sessions.\\n\\n## Source Pattern\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nClaude Brain's PostToolUse hook captures observations classified into 10 types with confidence scores and a 1-minute dedup window. SOURCE: ./research/context-management/claude-brain.md \u2192 Key Features \u2192 Automatic Observation Capture; Technical Architecture \u2192 PostToolUse Hook.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nExtend `task_status_hook.py` (or add a sibling `observation_capture_hook.py` registered alongside it) to classify each `PostToolUse` event into one of 10 observation types using rule-based heuristics and persist a structured observation record to `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/observations/<session-id>.jsonl`. Each record contains:\\n\\n- `id`, `timestamp`, `tool`, `type` (one of: discovery, decision, problem, solution, pattern, warning, success, refactor, bugfix, feature), `summary`, `confidence` (0.0-1.0), `metadata.session_id`\\n- A 1-minute in-memory dedup window keyed by `(tool_name, hash(input))` so identical successive calls produce one record with `count` incremented\\n\\nAdd a `min_confidence` threshold (default 0.6) below which observations are dropped \u2014 matches claude-brain's `minConfidence: 0.6` default in src/types.ts lines 78-84.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAfter implementing the change, run a Claude Code session that performs a `Grep` and an `Edit`. Then run:\\n\\n```bash\\nls ~/.dh/projects/-home-user-claude_skills/observations/\\n# Expect: <session-id>.jsonl exists\\n\\ncat ~/.dh/projects/-home-user-claude_skills/observations/<session-id>.jsonl | jq -r '.type' | sort -u\\n# Expect output includes at least one of: discovery, solution, bugfix\\n```\\n\\nField `confidence` present in every record. Identical tool calls within 60 seconds collapse to one record with `count: N` instead of N records.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` lines 58-67 register `task_status_hook.py` as the only PostToolUse handler, scoped to `Write|Edit|Bash`. Lines 854 and 929-933 of that script show the handler's sole responsibility on PostToolUse is to update a `LastActivity` timestamp on the active task file. Grep for `classify`, `observation`, `confidence`, `dedup`, or `categorize` against `task_status_hook.py` returns matches only inside the LastActivity-write logic \u2014 the hook does not classify the tool output, does not record what kind of work was done, and does not store an observation record.\\n\\nConsequences:\\n\\n- The orchestrator and downstream tooling have no record of which tool calls produced a `discovery` (e.g., a Grep that found a file), a `solution` (an Edit that resolved an error), or a `bugfix` (a commit that fixed a failing test). The signal exists in the JSONL transcript but is not extracted, classified, or made queryable.\\n- Periodic knowledge auto-save (#1678) and PreCompact context preservation (#1677) \u2014 when those land \u2014 will save raw snapshots, but without per-tool-call observation classification they cannot deliver the \\\"search past decisions/bugs/solutions by type\\\" capability claude-brain provides.\\n- Repeated tool calls within a tight loop are written to LastActivity verbatim with no dedup window, so a Bash command run 5 times in 30 seconds creates 5 timestamp updates instead of one observation with `count: 5`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Relationship To Existing Items\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nComplements #1678 (periodic auto-save counter) and #1677 (PreCompact context preservation) \u2014 those persist raw snapshots; this item adds per-tool-call typed observations that make snapshots queryable by intent (decision/bug/solution).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Rt-Ica Assessment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING**\\n\\nAll required inputs are present from primary sources. No human input needed.\\n\\n| Input | Status | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Item description \u2014 extend PostToolUse hook to classify and persist typed observations |\\n| Scope boundaries | AVAILABLE | 10 type values, 1-min dedup window, 0.6 min_confidence, JSONL output path |\\n| External interfaces | AVAILABLE | hooks.json lines 58-67, task_status_hook.py lines 853-933 |\\n| Constraints | AVAILABLE | 10-second hook timeout \u2192 rule-based heuristics only; PEP 723 Python 3.11+; uv run --script |\\n| Existing system context | AVAILABLE | context file mechanism confirmed; dh_paths slug resolution in use |\\n| Verification expectations | AVAILABLE | Measurable Signal section specifies exact commands and expected output |\\n</div>\\n\\n## Blockers\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nNone \u2014 all inputs are present. The implementation can proceed directly to planning.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Rt Ica Assessment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING**\\n\\nAll required inputs are present from primary sources. No human input needed.\\n\\n| Input | Status | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Item description \u2014 extend PostToolUse hook to classify and persist typed observations |\\n| Scope boundaries | AVAILABLE | 10 type values, 1-min dedup window, 0.6 min_confidence, JSONL output path |\\n| External interfaces | AVAILABLE | hooks.json lines 58-67, task_status_hook.